{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TX4JF5Nh136HNnFxf5BypJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Revamp â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\ttest-command: python -m pytest\n4\t\n5\t**North Star:** Make Aurora deliver felt, trustworthy value AND run on a robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture â€” co-equal goals. Success = John sees the reports, can navigate the library, Helping Hand surfaces, he gets a digestible KG summary, trusts the cost numbers, and curation quality (esp. source-quality weighting) + run-robustness improve via the new engine. Substrate: metered API is default (cost bug fixed via thinking_budget=0); flat-rate Claude Max + Gemini Ultra are an optional spike-gated transport, never the foundation; embeddings stay on API. Use the Foreman/Crucible PATTERN (fresh-context sub-agents + adversarial EXECUTEâ†’REVIEWâ†’FIX), NOT its wave-to-done engine. Locked-preserved: KB schema + library, security gating, deterministic cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher.\n6\t\n7\t## Success criteria\n8\t- John sees the morning briefing without opening a folder.\n9\t- The library is navigable (real domain Ã— complexity, not \"(unplaced) ? (?)\").\n10\t- Helping Hand surfaces matches in a Cowork session.\n11\t- Each curation carries a verified/documented/lossy confidence badge (source-quality signal).\n12\t- Cost numbers are trustworthy: every LLM call metered against a matching pricing key.\n13\t- The discovery swarm prioritizes high-yield sources while still exploring new ones.\n14\t- Locked assets (KB schema + library, security gating, cost telemetry, Helping Hand + publisher) remain intact.\n15\t\n16\t> Every wave ships real source its new tests import and exercise; acceptance criteria follow the D16 hybrid convention (a one-line done-when + Given/When/Then for non-trivial waves).\n17\t\n18\t## Wave 1 â€” Make the output visible\n19\t\n20\t**Intent:** Close the consume-loop bridges so John actually sees Auroraâ€™s output.\n21\t\n22\t**Deliverables:** Deliver the morning briefing where John lives (toast / email / auto-surfaced session note); Fix the library/index.md domainÃ—complexity join (currently renders \"(unplaced) ? (?)\" for all rows)\n23\t\n24\t**Depends on:** â€”\n25\t\n26\t**done-when:** John receives the briefing without opening a folder, and library/index.md shows real domain/complexity for â‰¥95% of placed artifacts.\n27\t\n28\t- **Given** a completed nightly sweep, **when** the briefing job runs, **then** John receives a notification containing the top finds\n29\t- **Given** the KB has placed embeddings, **when** library/index.md is regenerated, **then** â‰¥95% of placed artifacts show a real domain and complexity (not \"(unplaced) ? (?)\")\n30\t\n31\t## Wave 2 â€” Security-gate single-owner + backfill\n32\t\n33\t**Intent:** Make the fail-closed gate predicate single-owner and populate security_status (the converged Shark/landmine finding).\n34\t\n35\t**Deliverables:** De-duplicate gate_predicate_sql() literal into one owner (roles/security/gate.py); import it at all enforcement points; CI grep test failing if the servable literal appears outside gate.py; Backfill security_status (currently NULL on all artifacts)\n36\t\n37\t**Depends on:** Make the output visible\n38\t\n39\t**done-when:** The servable literal exists in exactly one file (CI test passes) and no artifact has NULL security_status.\n40\t\n41\t- **Given** the repo, **when** the gate-predicate CI test runs, **then** the security_status servable literal is found in exactly one file (gate.py)\n42\t- **Given** the KB, **when** security_status is backfilled, **then** no artifact row has NULL security_status and enforce-mode no longer empties MCP queries\n43\t\n44\t## Wave 3 â€” Evidence-rigor fix-loop and confidence badge\n45\t\n46\t**Intent:** Add an adversarial EXECUTEâ†’REVIEWâ†’FIXâ†’RE-REVIEW loop that iterates EVIDENCE (never the verdict), emitting a verified/documented/lossy badge.\n47\t\n48\t**Deliverables:** Deterministic evidence-deepener (expand corpus by next N chars / referenced files in declared order; never LLM-chosen excerpts); Loop exit conditions: disagreement â‰¤0.4 â†’ reduce; MAX_EVIDENCE_ITERS without convergence â†’ force-downgrade to flag; any injection_riskâ‰¥0.7 or reject vote â†’ reject; Confidence badge derivation (verified/documented/lossy) + surface it with the incorporation note in the briefing and Helping Hand; Shadow-run mode (validations_shadow) + engine-diff harness with the promotion gate\n49\t\n50\t**Depends on:** Security-gate single-owner + backfill\n51\t\n52\t**done-when:** Each curation carries a verified/documented/lossy badge from an evidence-iterating loop, no path produces unearned pass, the badge shows in the briefing + Helping Hand, and the shadow-run diff meets the promotion gate.\n53\t\n54\t- **Given** a candidate with disagreeing critics, **when** the fix-loop runs, **then** it expands the evidence corpus deterministically and re-scores, never re-prompting critics to pass\n55\t- **Given** a candidate that fails to converge within MAX_EVIDENCE_ITERS, **when** the loop exits, **then** the verdict is force-downgraded to flag (never pass)\n56\t- **Given** a validated candidate, **when** the briefing or Helping Hand renders it, **then** its verified/documented/lossy badge and incorporation note are shown\n57\t\n58\t## Wave 4 â€” Trustworthy cost numbers\n59\t\n60\t**Intent:** Make the cost ledger reflect real spend (the $118 incident class).\n61\t\n62\t**Deliverables:** Replace the UNVERIFIED pricing.yaml guesses with real Google/Anthropic SKU rates; Meter the MCP server query-embedding path (server.py:_embed_query), currently unmetered; Regression test asserting the model tag used at call time matches a pricing.yaml key\n63\t\n64\t**Depends on:** Evidence-rigor fix-loop and confidence badge\n65\t\n66\t**done-when:** Every LLM call is metered against a pricing.yaml key that matches the model tag used at call time, verified by a regression test.\n67\t\n68\t- **Given** a nightly run, **when** costs roll up, **then** every callâ€™s model tag resolves to a pricing.yaml key (no $0 fiction), asserted by a regression test\n69\t- **Given** a Helping Hand query, **when** it embeds the query, **then** the embedding call is metered into the costs table\n70\t\n71\t## Wave 5 â€” Scout memory and source-reputation\n72\t\n73\t**Intent:** Give the discovery swarm memory â€” prioritize high-yield sources while still exploring new ones; surface source quality (Johnâ€™s addition; down-payment on the learning loop).\n74\t\n75\t**Deliverables:** Per-source yield tracking (which sources produced accepted/verified artifacts vs noise); Explore/exploit seed prioritization respecting the existing 2-curator + 3-night-shadow promotion rule; Source-quality indicator per artifact in the library + briefing\n76\t\n77\t**Depends on:** Trustworthy cost numbers\n78\t\n79\t**done-when:** Scout passes prioritize historically high-yield sources, spend a measurable budget on new exploration, and each artifact shows a source-quality indicator.\n80\t\n81\t- **Given** N nights of yield history, **when** a sweep plans its scout pass, **then** high-yield sources are prioritized and a measurable exploration budget is allocated to new sources\n82\t- **Given** an artifact, **when** the library or briefing renders it, **then** a source-quality indicator is shown\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f57f8c55-258c-429e-9481-a8b3d3286294","uuid":"8b7a143e-6884-439b-8d06-9c4eea2fc35b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:52:12.454Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\foreman-handoff\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md","content":"# Aurora Revamp â€” Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n\ntest-command: python -m pytest\n\n**North Star:** Make Aurora deliver felt, trustworthy value AND run on a robust Foreman/Crucible-style agentic architecture â€” co-equal goals. Success = John sees th